 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[36,37],"#Development of deep-learning tool to predict appropriate height and weight from chest radiographs in bedridden patients#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[38,40],"#Development of deep-learning tool to predict appropriate height and weight from chest radiographs in bedridden patients#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[39,40],"#Development of deep-learning tool to predict appropriate height and weight from chest radiographs in bedridden patients#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/55QME7ZY","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/NKZAY27V?page=1&annotation=H2DKV6TX","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/NKZAY27V?page=1&annotation=SCLYD6PR","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/NKZAY27V?page=2&annotation=W6AA79V7","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/NKZAY27V?page=2&annotation=2T7NKGM6","line":39}],"metadata":{"Title":"Development of deep-learning tool to predict appropriate height and weight from chest radiographs in bedridden patients","Authors":"Yasuhiko Nakao, Ryo Sasaki, Fumihiro Mawatari, Kotaro Harakawa, Minoru Okita, Norisato Mitsutake, Kazuhiko Nakao","Year":2023,"DOI":"10.1016/j.nutos.2023.08.005","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"This study aimed to illustrate the potential of a convolutional neural network model to assess the height and weight based on chest radiographs.A convolutional neural network was used to predict the height and weight of the patients (Juzen NST). A ResNet152 classifier was trained using Fastai (V1.0) running on PyTorch to predict the height and weight. Training was performed for four epochs using validation without augmentation.","Findings":"Our chest radiographic prediction model has a high correlation with actual height and weight and can be combined with information regarding clinical nutrition factors for rapid assessment of risk for malnutrition","Conclusions":"area. Importantly, our model is an illustration of the potential of automated imaging artificial intelligence for proper nutrition prediction models in older adults.","Limitations":"","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"b6ab6w","at":1774939552126}},"smart_blocks:Augmented Dietitian Okunmuşlar/nakaoDevelopmentDeeplearningTool2023a.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.0649552,0.01728538,-0.00614021,0.01575381,0.01609513,0.00877199,-0.01738158,0.01594107,-0.00832326,0.00562081,0.00234866,-0.11078712,-0.0198867,0.06802042,0.05641547,-0.01036948,0.04050549,0.0332527,-0.03075883,0.02626768,0.05604463,0.01518211,0.01975622,-0.03968934,0.08160608,-0.04436727,-0.00071055,-0.06316832,-0.06016884,-0.22916222,0.06808698,-0.03299614,0.08945052,-0.01594815,-0.04178488,0.0147382,0.00089611,0.04456991,-0.02828059,0.0312712,0.00366242,0.04389488,0.01598908,-0.00848461,0.04308311,-0.02656713,-0.02944883,-0.05909394,-0.03755119,0.05428058,-0.02838213,-0.04027099,0.02484716,0.06598999,0.03311732,-0.00970364,0.0540098,0.02173505,0.06777719,0.07184587,-0.00123416,0.08010732,-0.20418897,0.05886766,0.02332646,0.03792091,-0.05010804,0.00984015,0.03226023,0.01277501,0.01399824,0.03096295,0.06294073,0.03899875,-0.0001078,0.00600964,0.02425781,-0.02853151,0.00384486,-0.0310037,0.00770533,0.07680744,-0.04887014,-0.0340787,-0.04416878,-0.03243994,-0.02413391,-0.06543781,0.0004821,-0.01901881,-0.05331342,-0.03700497,-0.04884908,0.03563649,-0.03466756,-0.00137711,0.03620082,0.00677973,-0.09223931,0.09930892,-0.01842735,0.01771893,0.03127102,0.00561223,0.04152057,-0.06005578,-0.04830839,-0.04873173,0.00428287,0.04502416,-0.04092992,0.0029362,-0.03987417,0.01845214,-0.01220989,0.04501182,0.07574354,0.05756917,-0.00754135,-0.00177255,-0.